WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.478
The most common occurrence of a lightning
event is known as a thunderstorm, though

00:00:04.478 --> 00:00:08.956
they can also commonly occur in other
types of energetic weather systems, such

00:00:08.956 --> 00:00:13.434
as volcanic eruptions. Positive lightning
has also been shown to trigger the

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:17.912
occurrence of upward lightning flashes
from the tops of tall structures and is

00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:22.390
largely responsible for the initiation of
sprites several tens of kilometers above

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:26.868
ground level. The electrification of
volcanic ash plumes and the occurrence of

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:31.345
volcanic lightning are now known to be
common phenomena during explosive volcanic

00:00:31.345 --> 00:00:35.824
eruptions. The most direct effects of
lightning on humans occur as a result of

00:00:35.824 --> 00:00:40.302
cloud-to-ground lightning, even though
intra-cloud and cloud-to-cloud are more

00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:44.780
common. Contrary to popular belief,
positive lightning flashes do not

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.257
necessarily originate from the anvil or
the upper positive charge region and

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:53.736
strike a rain-free area outside of the
thunderstorm.

00:00:53.736 --> 00:00:58.148
Positive lightning produces both higher
peak currents and longer continuing

00:00:58.148 --> 00:01:02.561
currents, making them capable of heating
surfaces to much higher levels which

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:06.973
increases the likelihood of a fire being
ignited. The conductivity of the

00:01:06.973 --> 00:01:11.386
electrical ground, be it soil, fresh
water, or salt water, may affect the

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:15.798
lightning discharge rate and thus visible
characteristics. Positive lightning is

00:01:15.798 --> 00:01:20.211
less common than negative lightning and on
average makes up less than 5% of all

00:01:20.211 --> 00:01:24.624
lightning strikes. The long distances
positive lightning can propagate through

00:01:24.624 --> 00:01:29.036
clear air explains why they are known as
"bolts from the blue", giving no warning

00:01:29.036 --> 00:01:33.449
to observers. Several past studies have
reported on observational findings

00:01:33.449 --> 00:01:37.861
regarding how charge structures relate to
different lightning types over a wide

00:01:37.861 --> 00:01:42.274
range of convective regimes. Possible
sites of electro-optical activity are

00:01:42.274 --> 00:01:46.686
noted—eolian and volcanic discharges near
the surface, convective lightning in the

00:01:46.686 --> 00:01:51.099
cloud layer, and possible transient
luminous events like sprites in the

00:01:51.099 --> 00:01:55.512
mesosphere.

00:01:55.512 --> 00:02:00.502
Most CG lightning is negative, meaning
that a negative charge is transferred

00:02:00.502 --> 00:02:05.492
(electrons flow) downwards to ground along
the lightning channel (the conventional

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:10.482
current flows from the ground up to the
cloud). Positive and negative lightning

00:02:10.482 --> 00:02:15.473
Cloud-to-ground (CG) lightning is either
positive or negative, as defined by the

00:02:15.473 --> 00:02:20.463
direction of the conventional electric
current between cloud and ground. The

00:02:20.463 --> 00:02:25.453
reverse happens in a positive CG flash,
where electrons travel upward along the

00:02:25.453 --> 00:02:30.444
lightning channel, while also a positive
charge is transferred downward to the

00:02:30.444 --> 00:02:35.434
ground (the conventional current travels
from cloud to ground). We have analyzed

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:40.424
very high frequency lightning mapping
observations and remote magnetic field

00:02:40.424 --> 00:02:45.414
measurements to investigate connections
between lightning morphology and impulse

00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:50.405
charge moment change (iCMC) of negative
cloud‐to‐ground (CG) strokes with high

00:02:50.405 --> 00:02:55.395
estimated peak currents. An average bolt
of negative lightning creates an electric

00:02:55.395 --> 00:03:00.385
current of 30,000 amperes (30 kA),
transferring a total 15 C (coulombs) of

00:03:00.385 --> 00:03:05.376
electric charge and 1 gigajoule of energy.

00:03:05.376 --> 00:03:10.251
According to observations, the energy
density contained inside ball lightning

00:03:10.251 --> 00:03:15.126
can reach 1010 J/m3, and its charge can
range from 10−3 to 10−1 C. Apart from

00:03:15.126 --> 00:03:20.002
lightning diagnostic schemes producing
bulk flash metrics such as average

00:03:20.002 --> 00:03:24.877
lightning activity with useful skill up to
several days forecast, some studies have

00:03:24.877 --> 00:03:29.753
focused on assessment of the lightning
threat in the very near future and

00:03:29.753 --> 00:03:34.628
providing early warning by nowcasting
individual flashes and/or the onset of

00:03:34.628 --> 00:03:39.504
lightning within the storm. Positive
lightning strikes tend to be much more

00:03:39.504 --> 00:03:44.379
intense than their negative counterparts.
As a result of their greater power,

00:03:44.379 --> 00:03:49.254
positive lightning strikes are
considerably more dangerous than negative

00:03:49.254 --> 00:03:54.130
strikes. Positive lightning tends to occur
more frequently in winter storms, as with

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:59.005
thundersnow, during intense tornadoes and
in the dissipation stage of a

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:03.881
thunderstorm. Recent experimental evidence
has correlated IBPs to the initial

00:04:03.881 --> 00:04:08.756
development of lightning leaders inside
the thundercloud. The produced warnings

00:04:08.756 --> 00:04:13.632
are validated using the data from
lightning location systems.

00:04:13.632 --> 00:04:18.154
Since lightning involves complex
interactions between many atmospheric and

00:04:18.154 --> 00:04:22.676
in-cloud processes, it is unsurprising
that research into that phenomenon

00:04:22.676 --> 00:04:27.198
continues to generate a wide range of
approaches for its prediction. Four

00:04:27.198 --> 00:04:31.721
lightning morphologies are identified for
a total of 2126 strokes within optimum

00:04:31.721 --> 00:04:36.243
detection range of the North Alabama
Lightning Mapping Array, and statistical

00:04:36.243 --> 00:04:40.765
iCMC distributions are given for each of
these types. Despite several different

00:04:40.765 --> 00:04:45.288
approaches applied to the important
problem of lightning nowcasting and early

00:04:45.288 --> 00:04:49.810
warning generation, the complex processes
and large number of parameters involved in

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:54.332
the problem lends themselves to the
potential application of a machine

00:04:54.332 --> 00:04:58.854
learning approach. Many other
observational variants are recognized,

00:04:58.854 --> 00:05:03.377
including: volcanic lightning, which can
occur during volcanic eruptions; "heat

00:05:03.377 --> 00:05:07.899
lightning", which can be seen from a great
distance but not heard; dry lightning,

00:05:07.899 --> 00:05:12.421
which can cause forest fires; and ball
lightning, which is rarely observed

00:05:12.421 --> 00:05:16.944
scientifically.

00:05:16.944 --> 00:05:21.708
Lightning involves a near-instantaneous
release of energy on a scale averaging

00:05:21.708 --> 00:05:26.472
between 200 megajoules and 7 gigajoules.
We have used machine learning techniques

00:05:26.472 --> 00:05:31.236
to successfully hindcast nearby and
distant lightning hazards by looking at

00:05:31.236 --> 00:05:36.000
single-site observations of meteorological
parameters. Third, lightning may be

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.764
important in atmospheric evolution and
prebiotic evolution, notably in fixing

00:05:40.764 --> 00:05:45.528
nitrogen which is an essential element in
living things but is generally chemically

00:05:45.528 --> 00:05:50.292
inaccessible. Most NBEs are quite peculiar
in the sense that very frequently they

00:05:50.292 --> 00:05:55.056
occur in isolation from other lightning
processes. The results encourage further

00:05:55.056 --> 00:05:59.820
analysis on how mining techniques could
contribute to further our understanding of

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:04.584
lightning dependencies on atmospheric
parameters. Based on the reports for 1023

00:06:04.584 --> 00:06:09.348
fatalities associated with natural hazard
processes in Switzerland during the period

00:06:09.348 --> 00:06:14.112
from 1946 to 2015, more than 16% of the
cases were caused by lightning, making it

00:06:14.112 --> 00:06:18.876
the second most frequent cause of loss of
life among the natural hazards in

00:06:18.876 --> 00:06:23.640
Switzerland.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:28.639
Lightning initiation problem is solved by
GRBs that slam into thunderclouds and

00:06:28.639 --> 00:06:33.638
carve a conductive path through a
thunderstorm. To date the true nature of

00:06:33.638 --> 00:06:38.638
initial breakdown pulses (IBPs) and narrow
bipolar events (NBEs) in lightning

00:06:38.638 --> 00:06:43.637
discharges remains a mystery. Fortunately
not all of them kill people, albeit 10%

00:06:43.637 --> 00:06:48.636
people fall prey to lightning annually,
out of which hardly 20 to 25% die.

00:06:48.636 --> 00:06:53.636
Finally, lightning may be a hazard for
vehicles exploring a planetary atmosphere.

00:06:53.636 --> 00:06:58.635
Lightning also causes thunder, a sound
from the shock wave which develops as

00:06:58.635 --> 00:07:03.635
heated gases in the vicinity of the
discharge experience a sudden increase in

00:07:03.635 --> 00:07:08.634
pressure. Witnesses often report seeing
moving sparks about one millimeter in size

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:13.633
inside the ball lightning shell. Lightning
preventive, alerting and control devices

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:18.633
help reduce fatality rates by the bolts
out of blue skies. Power and energy

00:07:18.633 --> 00:07:23.632
lifelines such as transmission lines, oil
tankers and gas or petroleum pipelines are

00:07:23.632 --> 00:07:28.632
susceptible to lightning strikes.

00:07:28.632 --> 00:07:33.507
Artificial rocket and laser triggered
lightning protection and control

00:07:33.507 --> 00:07:38.382
techniques help to divert the lightning
attacks. The VHF Broadband Digital

00:07:38.382 --> 00:07:43.257
Interferometer developed by Osaka
University has been improved to allow

00:07:43.257 --> 00:07:48.132
continuous sampling over the entire
duration of a lightning flash and to

00:07:48.132 --> 00:07:53.008
utilize a generalized cross-correlation
technique for determining the lightning

00:07:53.008 --> 00:07:57.883
source directions. The air around the
lightning flash rapidly heats to

00:07:57.883 --> 00:08:02.758
temperatures of about 30,000 °C (54,000
°F). Lightning is considered an Essential

00:08:02.758 --> 00:08:07.633
Climate Variable by the World
Meteorological Organization, and its

00:08:07.633 --> 00:08:12.508
scientific study is called fulminology.
Lightning warning systems in parks, sport

00:08:12.508 --> 00:08:17.384
complexes, schools, local government
buildings, airports, space centers, etc.

00:08:17.384 --> 00:08:22.259
benefit from the output of such lightning
nowcasting schemes to give decision-makers

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:27.134
enough time to make take the necessary
safety precautions for staff and visitors,

00:08:27.134 --> 00:08:32.009
stop lightning-sensitive operations, and
protect equipment. By merging the

00:08:32.009 --> 00:08:36.884
satellite and radar systems with numerical
models, the lightning forecast is made

00:08:36.884 --> 00:08:41.760
30–45 min before rainfall occurs.

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:46.333
Lightning influences the global
atmospheric electrical circuit and

00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:50.906
atmospheric chemistry and is a natural
ignition source of wildfires. Lightning

00:08:50.906 --> 00:08:55.479
was considered to be the second cause of
death making natural disasters after

00:08:55.479 --> 00:09:00.052
flashfloods but preventive measures have
slithered it down to the third place in

00:09:00.052 --> 00:09:04.625
developed countries. A key challenge is in
the interpretation of electrical or

00:09:04.625 --> 00:09:09.198
magnetic signatures claimed to be
whistler-mode emissions from lightning

00:09:09.198 --> 00:09:13.771
discharges. Lightning experts had hardly
developed any concurrence on lightning

00:09:13.771 --> 00:09:18.344
physics, and the observation of dark
lightning complicated the Gordian knot.

00:09:18.344 --> 00:09:22.917
However, lightning itself is viewed as an
extraterrestrial energy source. The

00:09:22.917 --> 00:09:27.490
negative sprite‐parent lightning took
place in two thunderstorms that were

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:32.064
associated with a tropical disturbance in
east central and south Florida.

00:09:32.064 --> 00:09:37.071
On average, 50 lightning strikes occur on
earth in one second. Cloud to ground (CG)

00:09:37.071 --> 00:09:42.078
Cloud-to-ground (CG) lightning is a
lightning discharge between a thundercloud

00:09:42.078 --> 00:09:47.085
and the ground. Given its noteworthy
socioeconomic impact, appreciable

00:09:47.085 --> 00:09:52.093
attention has been given to accurate
lightning prediction. Intra-cloud and

00:09:52.093 --> 00:09:57.100
cloud-to-cloud lightning indirectly affect
humans through their influence on

00:09:57.100 --> 00:10:02.107
atmospheric chemistry. There are a number
of mechanisms theorized to result in the

00:10:02.107 --> 00:10:07.114
formation of positive lightning. Large
bolts of positive lightning can create up

00:10:07.114 --> 00:10:12.122
to 120 kA and transfer 350 C. Lightning is
responsible for human injuries and

00:10:12.122 --> 00:10:17.129
fatalities, the death of livestock, and
house and forest fires. Lightning injures

00:10:17.129 --> 00:10:22.136
victims by heat, shockwave, intense
brightness, radio waves, and secondary

00:10:22.136 --> 00:10:27.144
slip or fall mechanisms.

00:10:27.144 --> 00:10:32.148
Lightning prevention rule recommends ‘when
the thunder roars, go indoors’. CG is the

00:10:32.148 --> 00:10:37.152
least common, but best understood of all
types of lightning.

00:10:37.152 --> 00:10:42.193
To date the true nature of initial
breakdown pulses (IBPs) and narrow bipolar

00:10:42.193 --> 00:10:47.235
events (NBEs) in lightning discharges
remains a mystery. Recent experimental

00:10:47.235 --> 00:10:52.277
evidence has correlated IBPs to the
initial development of lightning leaders

00:10:52.277 --> 00:10:57.318
inside the thundercloud. Most NBEs are
quite peculiar in the sense that very

00:10:57.318 --> 00:11:02.360
frequently they occur in isolation from
other lightning processes. Lightning

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:07.402
discharges in the atmosphere owe their
existence to the combination of complex

00:11:07.402 --> 00:11:12.444
dynamic and microphysical processes. We
have used machine learning techniques to

00:11:12.444 --> 00:11:17.485
successfully hindcast nearby and distant
lightning hazards by looking at

00:11:17.485 --> 00:11:22.527
single-site observations of meteorological
parameters. The produced warnings are

00:11:22.527 --> 00:11:27.569
validated using the data from lightning
location systems. The model also improves

00:11:27.569 --> 00:11:32.610
upon three competitive baselines for
generating lightning warnings: (i) a

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:37.652
simple but objective baseline forecast,
based on the persistence method, (ii) the

00:11:37.652 --> 00:11:42.694
widely-used method based on a threshold of
the vertical electrostatic field magnitude

00:11:42.694 --> 00:11:47.736
at ground level, and, finally (iii) a
scheme based on CAPE threshold.
